# INTRO
introSlug: milling
intro:
  heading: "Commercial Cold-Planing Asphalt Milling & Pavement Overlays"
  paragraphs:
    - >
      Asphalt milling is the most cost-effective method for restoring deteriorated commercial parking lots and roadways without disturbing underlying subgrade gravel. S. Phaneuf & Associates deploys commercial milling machinery to grind off damaged surface layers (1.5 to 3 inches deep), restoring proper drainage pitch and grade transitions.
    - >
      Milled asphalt material is reclaimed for recycled aggregate use. Following profile milling, our paving crews sweep the sub-base, apply a liquid tack coat bonding adhesive, and lay a dense 1.5-to-2 inch top course of hot-mix asphalt.
    - >
      Asphalt milling restores smooth pavement riding surfaces while preserving existing curb reveals, catch basin heights, and sidewalk thresholds.

